  "summary": "A hydraulic accumulator stores energy in compressed gas. In this bladder type a nitrogen-filled bladder sits inside a steel shell; when system pressure rises, oil enters and squeezes the bladder; when pressure falls, the gas pushes the oil back out. Used for energy storage, pulsation damping and emergency power.",
